{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "טמאים הם לכם", :translit "t'me'im hem lachem", :gloss "unclean they are to you"} {:he "ואת החזיר", :translit "v'et hachazir", :gloss "and the pig"} {:he "מבשרם לא תאכלו", :translit "mibsaram lo tocheilu", :gloss "from their flesh you shall not eat"} {:he "את זה תאכלו מכל אשר במים", :translit "et zeh tocheilu mikol asher bamayim", :gloss "this you may eat of all that is in the waters"} {:he "לא תאכלו", :translit "lo tocheilu", :gloss "you shall not eat"} {:he "את זה תאכלו", :translit "et zeh tocheilu", :gloss "this you may eat"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikh parshiyot: juxtaposition of adjacent verses yields legal inferences"} {:kind :other, :note "Second interpretation uses gzerah shavah-style verbal linkage between לא תאכלו in land-animal and water-animal contexts"}], :frame {:text "The prohibition against raising pigs is found at Mishnah Bava Kamma 7:7. The principle of semikhut parshiyot — deriving law from the Torah's juxtaposition of passages — is a recognized hermeneutical method discussed in the Talmud. The two interpretive readings Ba'al HaTurim offers, concerning fish derivatives and the reliability of the seller, relate to the laws of kosher slaughter and sale of fish innards treated in Chullin.", :sources ["Mishnah Bava Kamma 7:7" "Chullin"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikh parshiyot: juxtaposition of adjacent verses yields legal inferences", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Second interpretation uses gzerah shavah-style verbal linkage between לא תאכלו in land-animal and water-animal contexts", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:34.607243362Z", :model "glm-5.2"}